## Alternative: Archive Instead of Delete

If you're unsure about deleting, you could move them to a reference folder:

```bash
# Create archive directory
mkdir -p docs/widget_examples

# Move instead of delete
mv lib/core/widgets/app_button_examples.dart docs/widget_examples/
mv lib/core/widgets/app_card_examples.dart docs/widget_examples/
mv lib/core/widgets/app_list_tile_examples.dart docs/widget_examples/
mv lib/core/widgets/fairway_background_examples.dart docs/widget_examples/

# Add note
echo "# Widget Examples (Archived)" > docs/widget_examples/README.md
echo "These showcase widgets were moved out of lib/ because they're not used in production." >> docs/widget_examples/README.md
echo "They remain here for reference purposes." >> docs/widget_examples/README.md

# Commit
git add docs/widget_examples/
git add lib/core/widgets/README.md
git commit -m "chore: archive unused example widgets to docs/

Moved example widgets out of lib/ to reduce codebase size and maintenance burden.
Files remain available in docs/widget_examples/ for reference."
```

This keeps the files for future reference without impacting build time or maintenance.

